{"id":"ee7c4e8a31dc0b92","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function.md","title":"ZFC Inner3 Definable Skolem Function","display":"df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function — ZFC Inner3 Definable Skolem Function","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function","aliases":["58-df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function"],"display":"df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function — ZFC Inner3 Definable Skolem Function","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction]]","[[../batch03/58-df-assignment]]","[[../batch06/58-df-proper]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-inner3-definable-skolem-function — ZFC Inner3 Definable Skolem Function"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a9132c2c1a18acd1\" href=\"?note=a9132c2c1a18acd1\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model\">../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula\">../batch17/58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment\">../batch03/58-df-assignment</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"8935dcac821c0104\" href=\"?note=8935dcac821c0104\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-proper\">../batch06/58-df-proper</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function\">../batch16/58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,F\\in V\">\\(M,F\\in V\\)</span> (transitive ZFC-model carrier and uniform Skolem-function candidates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_\\in\">\\(\\Sigma_\\in\\)</span> (the one-relation membership signature, whose sole relation symbol has arity <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2\">\\(2\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak M\">\\(\\mathfrak M\\)</span> (the canonical membership structure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>, supplied by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)=M\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)=M\\)</span> (universe projection of that structure)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\)</span> (membership-language formula-code set, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula\">../batch17/58-df-formula</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathfrak M,\\Sigma_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathfrak M,\\Sigma_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\)</span> (typed satisfaction recursion, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathfrak M,s)\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathfrak M,s)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s[v\\mapsto a]\">\\(s[v\\mapsto a]\\)</span> (assignment predicate and update, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment\">../batch03/58-df-assignment</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-coded function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function\">../batch16/58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\\)</span> (transitive-model predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"a9132c2c1a18acd1\" href=\"?note=a9132c2c1a18acd1\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model\">../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (canonical finite-tuple assignment predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcInner3DefinableSkolemFunction}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcInner3DefinableSkolemFunction}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}inner3\\text{-}finite\\text{-}tuple\\text{-}assignment}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S(s,\\vec a,\\mathfrak M)\\leftrightarrow\n\\vec a\\in\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)^{&lt;\\omega}\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathfrak M,s)\\land\n\\forall i\\in\\operatorname{dom}(\\vec a)\\;(s(v_i)=\\vec a(i))\\land\n\\forall i\\in\\omega\\setminus\\operatorname{dom}(\\vec a)\\;(s(v_i)=\\varnothing)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}inner3\\text{-}finite\\text{-}tuple\\text{-}assignment}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S(s,\\vec a,\\mathfrak M)\\leftrightarrow\n\\vec a\\in\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)^{&lt;\\omega}\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathfrak M,s)\\land\n\\forall i\\in\\operatorname{dom}(\\vec a)\\;(s(v_i)=\\vec a(i))\\land\n\\forall i\\in\\omega\\setminus\\operatorname{dom}(\\vec a)\\;(s(v_i)=\\varnothing)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}inner3\\text{-}definable\\text{-}skolem\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcInner3DefinableSkolemFunction}_S(M,F)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(M)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}\\bigl(F,\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\times M^{&lt;\\omega},M\\bigr)\\land\n\\exists\\mathfrak M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat}\\;\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak M,M)\\land\n\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathfrak M,\\Sigma_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\;\\forall\\vec a\\in M^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\\exists s\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S(s,\\langle\\varnothing\\rangle^\\frown\\vec a,\\mathfrak M)\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\bigl(\\operatorname{Sat}(\\exists v_0\\,\\varphi,s)\\to\n\\operatorname{Sat}(\\varphi,s[v_0\\mapsto F(\\langle\\varphi,\\vec a\\rangle)])\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\;\\exists p\\in M\\;\n\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\;\\forall\\vec a\\in M^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\\forall b\\in M\\;\\exists r\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S(r,\\langle\\varphi,\\vec a,b,p\\rangle,\\mathfrak M)\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\bigl(F(\\langle\\varphi,\\vec a\\rangle)=b\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Sat}(\\psi,r)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}inner3\\text{-}definable\\text{-}skolem\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcInner3DefinableSkolemFunction}_S(M,F)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(M)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}\\bigl(F,\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\times M^{&lt;\\omega},M\\bigr)\\land\n\\exists\\mathfrak M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat}\\;\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak M,M)\\land\n\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathfrak M,\\Sigma_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\;\\forall\\vec a\\in M^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\\exists s\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S(s,\\langle\\varnothing\\rangle^\\frown\\vec a,\\mathfrak M)\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\bigl(\\operatorname{Sat}(\\exists v_0\\,\\varphi,s)\\to\n\\operatorname{Sat}(\\varphi,s[v_0\\mapsto F(\\langle\\varphi,\\vec a\\rangle)])\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\;\\exists p\\in M\\;\n\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\;\\forall\\vec a\\in M^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\\forall b\\in M\\;\\exists r\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{FiniteTupleAssignment}_S(r,\\langle\\varphi,\\vec a,b,p\\rangle,\\mathfrak M)\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\bigl(F(\\langle\\varphi,\\vec a\\rangle)=b\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Sat}(\\psi,r)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Formula codes and finite parameter tuples are genuine set inputs to one uniform function. The displayed tuple-assignment predicate fixes every unused variable to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varnothing\">\\(\\varnothing\\)</span>, so neither satisfaction clause hides an unselected assignment.</li>\n<li>The last conjunct requires the entire graph of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> to be defined over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(M,\\in)\">\\((M,\\in)\\)</span> by one membership-language formula and one parameter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\in M\">\\(p\\in M\\)</span>, not separately formula by formula.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model","status":"resolved","id":"a9132c2c1a18acd1","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-assignment","status":"resolved","id":"64f35ba2e87964e0","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-assignment]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-proper","status":"resolved","id